{% if profile != 'frontend' %}## API examples

Health endpoints do not require authentication:

```bash
curl http://localhost:8000/health/live
curl http://localhost:8000/health/ready
```

{% if sample and not auth %}Create and query a sample item:

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/items \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"name":"First item","description":"Created from curl"}'

curl 'http://localhost:8000/api/v1/items?name=First&sort=createdAtDesc'
```
{% endif %}

{% if auth %}Create a development user and persist the session cookies:

```bash
curl -i -c .cookies.txt \
  -H 'Origin: http://localhost:5173' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"email":"developer@example.com","password":"correct-horse-battery","workspaceName":"Personal"}' \
  http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/signup

curl -b .cookies.txt http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/session
curl -b .cookies.txt http://localhost:8000/api/v1/workspaces
```

Unsafe authenticated requests also require the readable CSRF cookie in `X-CSRF-Token`. The
generated frontend middleware adds it automatically.
{% endif %}{% endif %}

## Production Compose

Copy the root production environment file, replace every placeholder, then validate:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose config
docker compose up -d --build
```

The gateway binds to `127.0.0.1:8080` by default and is intended to run behind an external TLS
terminator.
{% if profile == 'frontend' and sample %}
Set `FRONTEND_API_UPSTREAM` to the API origin reachable from the gateway container.
{% endif %}{% if auth %}
Production auth fails closed unless origins use HTTPS, cookies are Secure, the database URL and
rate-limit secret are explicit, and `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` contains only controlled proxy IPs/CIDRs.
Signup defaults to disabled in production.
{% endif %}

## Evolve this repository

Run these commands only with a clean Git worktree:

```bash
project-forge features .
project-forge doctor .
project-forge update --check .
project-forge update .
```

Project Forge supports additive `add`/`enable` operations and does not remove capabilities. Update
conflicts preserve all managed files and create `.rej` files for manual resolution.

When the installed tool and project both report `0.2.0`, `update --check` cannot detect a refreshed
same-version template from the version string alone. To apply this runtime compatibility refresh,
reinstall the tool source, verify a clean worktree, and run the update directly:

```bash
uv tool upgrade --reinstall project-forge
git status --short
project-forge update .
python3 harness/check.py
```

Read `AGENTS.md` before editing. Use [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md) to find the architecture
rules for Service/UoW/Repository boundaries, SQL, migrations, i18n, authentication, and events.
